What helped.
On case-a, reading `prime_bench.py` and the two evaluator keys. The design-fork key requires the Director's sentence and has no field for the action. The complete key can pass on a test-count mention. The packet command verified custody of member 0163 without accepting it. Claimed file hashes matched.

On case-b, the manual hash of the captured payloads, the 13 snapshots, and both specimen packets, plus the unittest. The assisted packet then verified member 0167 on its own: custody complete, helper text `not accepted`, artifact checks none. That split is the useful one. The cycle view's no-return line is the dead reader. The packet view is the custody check.

What slowed.
The reader failure, repeated only as far as each assisted route's required first read and first record. Case-a also re-read once, because the contract asks for a re-read, and both reads failed the same way. Case-b did not journal a second read. Its day command calls `read()` when `--registration` is set, so the reader ran once more inside that process. A first case-a day raced the re-read and listed one read; a second day listed both. Case-b day raced inspect and does not list it. Neither day was run again to tidy the listing.

The case-a test module cannot start in this cut. Discovering that twice, once on each route, cost two short failures and no information the second time. After the checkpoint those commands were not run again.

What still required judgment.
Pass finished and goal complete are different. Case-a's own contract is the instrument that was built. The later method page says those three controls were not already in that code, and the keys confirm it, so the pass can be accepted while the comparison goal stays open. Case-b's contract is the mechanical packet. The code, the tests, and the stored packets do that job, so the goal is complete even though the sealed page still says Review PENDING and the reservation still says reservation only.

A green custody line is not acceptance. A red cycle line is not a missing return. The 28 live differences are not historical corruption; the packet's own word for them is changed-live-working-copy, and the module does not contain the word corruption.

